      "text": [
        " «لِأَنَّ اَللَّهَ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ جَعَلَ يَوْمَ اَلْجُمُعَةِ أَضْيَقَ اَلْأَيَّامِ» فَقِيلَ لَهُ وَ لِمَ جَعَلَهُ أَضْيَقَ اَلْأَيَّامِ قَالَ «لِأَنَّهُ لاَ يُعَذِّبُ اَلْمُشْرِكِينَ فِي ذَلِكَ اَلْيَوْمِ لِحُرْمَتِهِ عِنْدَهُ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.676 - Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) was asked about the sun’s stillness (or 'pause') every day and why there is no such stillness for it on Jumu’ah.\nImam (as) said: \"Because Allah (swt), the Mighty and Majestic, made Jumu’ah the most constricted (or significant) of the days.\"\nIt was then asked: \"And why did He make it the most constricted of days?\"\nImam (as) said: \"Because on that day He does not punish the polytheists, due to the sanctity it holds with Him.\""
        ]
      }
    },
